},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c78d5c7354537f235c1734f6a441cd04a5f369a967657cd5e0b86b4d6730659","compact":"c54253242bd65002f0cd3fe6bfb39af4193ab6fefae23ed149d140b89ae81925","nasal":"c5e74d9c0f7bb365402dc7cdb812e851015f14bb21c09a5255305c65c996799a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-36-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":36,"verse":7,"english":"This is the celestial Gangă she on whom Hutaśana will beget a son-the foe-subduing generalissimo of the celestials.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.772,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-37-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1036007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8e90faf0afcf807a9c3d2ba647463777a5c09be4a2509615884447a74b7e5510","compact":"da5a6015ee7a40ae4766762ca610f7a22c3d2e7d8359fb3ab5945bef9ea05d18","nasal":"6160abd0e2db31693a974fce225dafb94424e4df840360017424f7004b9e2fc0"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-36-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":36,"verse":8,"english":"And the elder daughter of the Mountain will consider that son as brought forth by Uma; and Uma also will, without doubt, look upon him with regard.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-37-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1036008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec285d747d59f9be2d9b5a39876cdae8790e4433129f5e1df1e689167d9cbff8","compact":"80d7a2fab548da206e9ad115ee0a3432755a6d90ec11136aad8f647ad887f1d8","nasal":"a4e4a783d837894b6af02359787a77f9c095cf062596ed480de0186d4ef38de7"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-36-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":36,"verse":9,"english":"Hearing these words of him o descendant of Raghu, the gods bowing to the Grand-sire, paid him homage.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-37-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1036009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fb93ac2c848c45671ff5a8c2fcaad96ce2d6f809016cf836c6eda9cfb4804187","compact":"3af77447c0fb37a39918aaa41c55f709cd0680aad705ac77d80fca98ec4b122e","nasal":"187bce1aefee50d96089cf9035d1872eaedc312954cfa0cbfb00d0befe5c20fe"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-36-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":36,"verse":10,"english":"Then, O Rama, repairing to the Kailasa mountain teeming with metals, the deities commissioned Agni with the view of having a son (born to him.)10","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.723,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-37-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1036010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7b4117e42d0bc372413a755e95f261892a16d905649cd370412156ed990fa4e2","compact":"9e5cec3471dddc57cd554a6697a77d2370e89703b5737d543854e627632d446b","nasal":"b307702d2a4e34a75bcd08f63c315e1c0f1dd2a4eb020ffdec9055da3074f42f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-36-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":36,"verse":11,"english":"‘Do you, O god, accomplish this work of the oddities! O you of mighty energy, do you discharge your energy into that daughter of the Mountain, Ganga.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-37-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1036011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"263d4adca13d9c7db6487d40cc6b5dc830a53e127dd4a77e4978c1b97980f611","compact":"50f31ed00bbebbf2c2e07878ae52a97faf5600b21a3b087da3f5d05f9949d37e","nasal":"866c1955950a9ca52d47d83b2f34e3ed68bd2d449f4f7844caeba9579cf07695"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-36-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":36,"verse":12,"english":"Thereupon giving his promise to the gods, Pavaka* (Fire) approached Ganga, saying, Do you, O Goddess, bear an embryo; for even this is the desire of the deities.","alignm